RUN(1)                         User Commands                          RUN(1)

NAME
    run - run a program image from a file

SYNOPSIS
    run PATH

DESCRIPTION
    Read the program image at PATH through the fs_server and hand it to
    the kernel to run. The kernel validates it with the same loader every
    program goes through: segments are never writable and executable at
    once, every bound is checked, and a relocation that does not resolve
    fails the load.

    The program receives the shell's filesystem, narrowed: its root and
    working directory, never wider than the shell's own, taken back when
    it ends. It inherits nothing else unless the shell grants it.

    A bare name such as `wc` is looked up in /bin without `run` (sh(1)).

SEE ALSO
    ps(1), sh(1), capabilities(7)
